Section 2: The call is coming from inside the house 📞
▸
Question 1

A few weeks ago, you joined a friend out of town to go to a cybersecurity conference. While there, you attended a talk that warned about the rise of double-extortion. After compromising a network and stealing the most sensitive data they could find, cybercriminals would threaten high-level executives with the release of the stolen data unless the company paid them. A refusal to comply would trigger the deployment of ransomware on the network. The criminals would then proceed to demand at least double the money they were asking for in the first place. The researcher pointed this threat actor was skilled and hard to detect, and very much active.

You decided you needed to look for traces of them as soon as you got into the office the following monday. A data leak, the company could handle. A full blown-out ransomware, on the other hand…

Find the email addresses for the CEO, CFO and CTO.

What is the subject of the email all three of them received?

let A=
Employees
| where role has_any ("CEO","CFO","CTO")
  | project email_addr, role;
Email
| join kind=inner A on $left.recipient == $right.email_addr
| summarize 
    Recipients = make_set(recipient),
    Roles = make_set(role),
    Count = count()
    by subject
| where Count >= 2

["otto_hoctavius@galaxyneura.tech","melon_husk@galaxyneura.tech","normie_ozborn@galaxyneura.tech"]

///Woopsie, the code for your secret chip is gone. Pay up if you want it back 😘 

